      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>As a member of Hatzoloh, I responded to the World Trade Center on the morning of September 11, 2001. Given the notable Jewish dimension to this human tragedy, I was motivated to compose an Azkarah, a memorial poem, for all its victims and heroes.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_69167_introduction"/>
      <j:conditional xml:id="osp_69167_notes">
        <tei:fs type="opensiddur:paratext">
          <tei:f name="include">
            <tei:binary value="true"/>
          </tei:f>
        </tei:fs>
      </j:conditional>
      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This memorial prayer by Dr. Moshe Sokolow was offered on the first anniversary of the 9/11 massacres on 10 September 2002. The resource was first shared online at the Lookstein Center website however, only a synopsis of the azkarah is currently preserved there.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_69167_notes"/>
